jobs.description:
In the role of Quality Control Specialist, you will take charge of preserving product quality at every step of the production cycle. Your key responsibilities involve:
- Carrying out precise measurements and sampling in line with predefined standards;
- Reviewing and authorizing product batches prior to their transfer to storage;
- Overseeing and ensuring quality consistency throughout different production phases;
- Conducting quality assessments based on the established quality plan;
- Ensuring defective products do not proceed into the supply chain.

 - Work full-time in a rotating 5-shift pattern (06:00–14:00, 14:00–22:00, 22:00–06:00);
- Earn a competitive salary of €3,236 monthly, which includes a 28.5% shift bonus;
- Receive a travel reimbursement of €0.23 per kilometer, with no upper limit;
- Access various opportunities to grow personally and professionally within the organization;
- Start saving for your pension from day one under Covebo;
- Enjoy 25 vacation days provided through Covebo;
- Benefit from an 8.33% holiday bonus via Covebo;
- Explore the chance to secure a permanent role with Canpack after your time with Covebo.

 - Excellent command of English, both verbal and written;
- Hands-on experience with tools and methods for quality assurance;
- Exceptional analytical abilities and attention to detail;
- Familiarity with safety protocols and hygiene standards;
- Skilled in using Microsoft Office programs.

 For over 30 years, Canpack Helmond has been a leader in the metal packaging industry. With a strong presence in Central and Eastern Europe and expanding into Western Europe, Asia, and Africa, they are one of the largest manufacturers of metal packaging worldwide. Their dedicated team of nearly 8,000 employees produces approximately 25 billion beverage cans, 28 billion bottle closures, 1 billion metal containers for the food and chemical industries, and 700 tons of glass packaging annually.

Banqueting Chef de PartieMandarin Oriental Conservatorium, Amsterdam is looking for a Chef de Partie to join our Banqueting, In-Room-Dining & Lounge kitchen.Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional. Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world's most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences.As Chef de Partie, you will be responsible for the following duties:
• You will be supervising the day-to-day operation of a designated section within the kitchen, overseeing all aspects of food production;
• Delivering highest levels of quality and precision, preparing dishes in line with recipes and standards;
• Maintaining highest levels of hygiene and cost control;
• You will act as a role model and mentor to the junior members in the kitchen brigade, guiding and supporting them in their development.As Chef de Partie we expect from you: 
• Recent/current experience in the same position to that of Chef de Partie for at least two years;
• A passionate and quality-driven approach to cooking;
• Teamwork;
• Good knowledge of English language (written and spoken);
• Familiar with hygiene code and HACCP regulations;
• Ability to work evenings and weekend shifts.Our commitment to you:
• A salary in scale VI of the Horeca CAO;
• Excellent career progression with an iconic, luxury, global hotel brand. A lot of our colleagues joined us at the beginning of their career and are now leading their own teams and divisions;
• Fantastic learning and development opportunities for all levels of staff
